    "filename": "English.pdf",
    "text": "[PAGE 1/1 – OCR angle=0°]\nSenate President Hun Sen addressed calls for Cambodia to retaliate after\nThai soldiers shot Cambodian civilians in Prey Chan village, killing one and\ninjuring three.\n\nSpeaking at the 33rd Congress of Buddhist Monks in Phnom Penh, Mr Hun\nSen cautioned that returning fire would likely cause more casualties on both\nsides and further jeopardize the ceasefire and the Kuala Lumpur Peace\nAgreement.\n\nHe said:\n\n“The incident in Prey Chan village—they want us to open fire immediately.\nNow, if we open fire immediately, what will be the outcome? Please answer.\nThey are inciting us to open fire, from one incident to another. They even\nshoot rubber bullets at us. They shoot almost every night. But the government\nhas advised us not to respond.”\n\n“Others say that they shot and killed people, and we have kept quiet. But let\nme ask you again: if we open fire, will only one person die and three people\nbe injured? It could be more than that. Thai people could also die. And we\ncould also die in Sisophon. Let’s speak clearly about that. We are not afraid of\nfighting, but we are asking what the outcome of fighting will be. It would\ndestroy the ceasefire agreement and the peace declaration. Others, you can\nspeak outside. May | ask, do you condemn those who shot and wounded\nCambodian people?”",
